  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Katine Produce Trading Project</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Sector: Agriculture. Crops - Maize and Groundnuts. Beneficiaries: 1940 Smallholder farmers, of whom 660 are women. Project Description: Katine Joint Farmers Cooperative Society Ltd. (KAJOFACO) is a registered farmers primary cooperative based in Soroti District. The cooperative aims to improve its smallholder members livelihoods through: increasing the production and quality of produce (grain); bulking; collective marketing; value addition; and access to markets. The cooperative has challenges that are limiting the growth of the business such as lack of modern production equipment (at farmer level), insufficient working capital to enable them trade in bigger volumes of produce and lack of transport to carry produce from aggregation centers to the main store. USADF funds will be provided to increase farmers access to production inputs, promoting wide adoption of good agricultural practices (GAPs), and improving post-harvest handling of produce. It will also help enhance produce aggregation, value addition/processing and increasing farmer access to profitable markets..</narrative>
  </description>
